# Quantum 02 — The harmonic oscillator by the shooting method
#
# (Griffiths §2.3 and Problem 2.55.)  An electron is bound in a parabolic
# potential V(x) = ½ m ω² x² with ħω = 1.000 eV (a model quantum dot).
# Solve  −ħ²/2m ψ'' + V ψ = E ψ  numerically for the four lowest levels and
# compare with E_n = ħω (n + ½).
#
# Method: V is even, so the eigenstates are even (ψ(0) = 1, ψ'(0) = 0) or
# odd (ψ(0) = 0, ψ'(0) = 1).  Integrate outward to x_max = 7 oscillator
# lengths (a = √(ħ/mω)).  Away from an eigenvalue ψ blows up to +∞ or −∞
# there; the sign flips as E crosses an eigenvalue: solve ψ(x_max) = 0 for E.

ħω = 1.000 eV
ω = ħω / ħ
a = √(ħ / (m_e ω))
x_max = 7 a
V(x) = ½ m_e ω² x²

# parity p = 0 for even states, 1 for odd
psi_end(E, p) =
    solve ψ'' = (2 m_e / ħ²) (V(x) - E) ψ
      with ψ(0 nm) = (1 - p) [nm^(-1/2)], ψ'(0 nm) = p [nm^(-3/2)]
      for x from 0 nm to x_max
    return ψ(x_max)

print "oscillator length a =", a in nm
# Walk up in E to bracket each level (see 01 for why), then refine with solve.
for p from 0 to 1
    found = 0
    E_lo = 0.05 eV
    while found < 2
        E_hi = E_lo + 0.1 eV
        if psi_end(E_lo, p) * psi_end(E_hi, p) < 0
            solve psi_end(E, p) = 0 for E from E_lo to E_hi
            n = 2 found + p
            found += 1
            print "n =", n, " E_shoot =", E in eV to 10 digits, " ħω(n+½) =", ħω (n + ½) in eV to 10 digits
        E_lo = E_hi

# The analytic ground state ψ₀ = (1/(π a²))^(1/4) exp(−x²/2a²):
# check ⟨V⟩ = ħω/4 (half the ground-state energy, the virial theorem).
ψ0(x) = (1 / (π a²))^(1/4) exp(-x² / (2 a²))
print "<V> in ground state =", ∫ V(x) ψ0(x)² dx from -∞ to ∞ in eV to 10 digits
